WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.229 --> 00:00:03.879
How worried are the former Soviet states and
Ukraine’s neighbors?

00:00:03.879 --> 00:00:08.120
Amid Russia’s ongoing invasion of Ukraine,
Conflict Zone heads to NATO’S front line:

00:00:08.120 --> 00:00:09.910
the Baltic states.

00:00:09.910 --> 00:00:14.440
They share borders with both Russia and Belarus,
and for years they’ve warned their allies

00:00:14.440 --> 00:00:20.320
to stop ‘pressing the snooze button’ on
the security threat posed by Vladimir Putin.

00:00:20.320 --> 00:00:25.030
My guest is Latvian Deputy Prime Minister
and Defense Minister, Artis Pabriks, he joins

00:00:25.030 --> 00:00:26.289
me online from Riga.

00:00:26.289 --> 00:00:33.510
“Our armed forces in Latvia, Estonia, Lithuania,
Poland, we are fully ready to defend our country

00:00:33.510 --> 00:00:35.489
and we have a very high motivation.”

00:00:35.489 --> 00:00:38.300
How far does he think Putin’s war will go?

00:00:38.300 --> 00:00:40.739
Could it extend beyond Ukraine’s borders?

00:00:40.739 --> 00:00:43.000
Might Putin use nuclear weapons?

00:00:43.000 --> 00:00:48.700
And are Latvia’s NATO allies doing enough
to shore up the eastern flank.

00:00:48.700 --> 00:00:57.620
Join me for all that and more on this special
edition of Conflict Zone.

00:00:57.620 --> 00:01:00.329
Minister Artis Pabriks, welcome to Conflict
Zone.

00:01:00.329 --> 00:01:02.780
Thank you.

00:01:02.780 --> 00:01:08.430
Ukrainian President Zelensky has said this
week, "if we are no more, then God forbid,

00:01:08.430 --> 00:01:11.830
Latvia, Lithuania, Estonia will be next."

00:01:11.830 --> 00:01:13.460
Are you next?

00:01:13.460 --> 00:01:19.760
Well, I believe that Ukrainians will win this
war, so there will be no next, hopefully.

00:01:19.760 --> 00:01:27.360
But of course, we understand that if Ukraine
falls, then the pressure on all the border

00:01:27.360 --> 00:01:31.110
countries with Russia will increase.

00:01:31.110 --> 00:01:37.340
That's kind of clear from analysis, but we
are ready for this and we very much hope that

00:01:37.340 --> 00:01:39.140
Ukrainians will hold.

00:01:39.140 --> 00:01:42.200
I'm wondering how you think the Ukrainians
will win the war.

00:01:42.200 --> 00:01:46.810
They've, they've called on NATO, for example,
to execute a no-fly zone, and it appears that

00:01:46.810 --> 00:01:49.350
that has indeed been ruled out.

00:01:49.350 --> 00:01:54.361
And when we look at your circumstances, for
example, when we just look at the map, you

00:01:54.361 --> 00:01:57.500
share a border with both Russia and Belarus.

00:01:57.500 --> 00:02:01.780
You and your allies in the Baltics are linked
to NATO's main territory by a land corridor

00:02:01.780 --> 00:02:05.180
that is just 60 kilometers wide.

00:02:05.180 --> 00:02:11.550
Back in 2016, NATO war games showed that Russia
would overrun the Baltics in under three days.

00:02:11.550 --> 00:02:13.969
Surely you must be feeling vulnerable right
now?

00:02:13.969 --> 00:02:17.480
Well, you know, yes.

00:02:17.480 --> 00:02:24.849
On the one hand, we are small countries bordering
a huge aggressor state, which is now waging

00:02:24.849 --> 00:02:26.879
war against Ukraine.

00:02:26.879 --> 00:02:32.290
But on the other hand, you know, one thing
is war games and computer programs.

00:02:32.290 --> 00:02:37.239
Another thing is real life, and you know that
many analysts, even in the West, have been

00:02:37.239 --> 00:02:43.319
thinking that also Russian troops will overrun
Ukraine very smoothly and will take Kyiv.

00:02:43.319 --> 00:02:45.420
But you see what is happening.

00:02:45.420 --> 00:02:51.030
So from that perspective, I think life always
shows a difference.

00:02:51.030 --> 00:02:56.670
But there is a huge difference between Ukraine
and, for instance, my country, Latvia, because

00:02:56.670 --> 00:02:59.330
we are still members of European Union and
NATO.

00:02:59.330 --> 00:03:00.330
Right.

00:03:00.330 --> 00:03:05.719
And any kind of aggression towards us would
mean that there will be an all-over war.

00:03:05.719 --> 00:03:11.469
And we've, we've heard statements iterated
by NATO.

00:03:11.469 --> 00:03:16.359
For example, we heard [Secretary General Jens]
Stoltenberg saying that "every ally and every

00:03:16.359 --> 00:03:19.219
inch of NATO territory will indeed be defended."

00:03:19.219 --> 00:03:24.110
I'm just wondering how convinced you are right
now that your NATO allies will indeed be able

00:03:24.110 --> 00:03:26.090
to ensure your security.

00:03:26.090 --> 00:03:31.200
Even it comes if it comes to the cost of a
full-scale war with disastrous consequences

00:03:31.200 --> 00:03:37.530
because the West has wasted no time praising
itself for unity in this crisis.

00:03:37.530 --> 00:03:41.200
But are you convinced that will last in the
long haul?

00:03:41.200 --> 00:03:49.159
Well, first of all, one of the reasons why
Russians invaded Ukraine was that in previous

00:03:49.159 --> 00:03:56.730
conflicts — Georgian War 2008, Crimea annexation
in 2014 — the West was not sending strong

00:03:56.730 --> 00:03:59.030
signals enough to Russia.

00:03:59.030 --> 00:04:04.900
So Russians wrongly estimated that if they
invade Ukraine, the life will go on as usual.

00:04:04.900 --> 00:04:10.900
And this is what Medvedev also told in this
pre-staged Security Council meeting about

00:04:10.900 --> 00:04:12.209
10 days ago.

00:04:12.209 --> 00:04:17.090
Now that appeared to be wrong because [Russian
President Vladimir] Putin united the West.

00:04:17.090 --> 00:04:24.450
Now, as far as our conviction, a conviction
about Article 5, look, we are going here double

00:04:24.450 --> 00:04:25.450
track.

00:04:25.450 --> 00:04:31.820
First of all, our armed forces in Latvia,
Estonia, Lithuania, Poland, we are fully ready

00:04:31.820 --> 00:04:35.120
to defend our country and we have a very high
motivation.

00:04:35.120 --> 00:04:41.070
Secondly, on 24th of February, when I was
woken up shortly before four o'clock in the

00:04:41.070 --> 00:04:48.580
morning when Russian aggression started, four
hours later, already American Airborne Battalion

00:04:48.580 --> 00:04:50.220
landed in Latvia.

00:04:50.220 --> 00:04:55.350
That's a proof [that] Article 5 holds and
as we talk now, we have also American commander

00:04:55.350 --> 00:04:57.830
here in Latvia, which tells me the same.

00:04:57.830 --> 00:05:00.620
We are one.

00:05:00.620 --> 00:05:07.400
But Article 5 aside, let me ask you, Russia
has demanded, for example, prior to this invasion,

00:05:07.400 --> 00:05:12.120
they demanded a legally-binding agreement
to exclude Ukraine and Georgia from NATO membership

00:05:12.120 --> 00:05:16.740
and restrict NATO exercises and deployment
of various weapons in states bordering Russia,

00:05:16.740 --> 00:05:20.020
states such as your own, states, such as Latvia.

00:05:20.020 --> 00:05:25.760
Before the invasion of Ukraine, some of your
allies in NATO, including French President

00:05:25.760 --> 00:05:30.430
[Emmanuel] Macron, hinted at the need to acknowledge
Russia's security concerns.

00:05:30.430 --> 00:05:32.030
So there's unity now.

00:05:32.030 --> 00:05:35.610
But could members make compromises if they're
pushed?

00:05:35.610 --> 00:05:42.390
Well, they were mistaken then, because it's
very clear that there can't be made compromises

00:05:42.390 --> 00:05:44.060
on our liberty, our freedom.

00:05:44.060 --> 00:05:49.180
And if somebody wants to make concessions
or compromises, they should only speak about

00:05:49.180 --> 00:05:50.190
themselves.

00:05:50.190 --> 00:05:52.030
Now anyway, this stuff is over.

00:05:52.030 --> 00:05:58.160
And of course, the Russian ultimatum, let's
say, proposed to NATO in those days, was clearly

00:05:58.160 --> 00:06:04.630
only was one idea: that they understood that
NATO countries like mine, we simply cannot

00:06:04.630 --> 00:06:09.190
accept such ultimatum because that would simply
mean to open borders to Russians.

00:06:09.190 --> 00:06:13.260
It would be just the same if we would ask
Russians to withdraw all the troops behind

00:06:13.260 --> 00:06:14.260
the Ural Mountains.

00:06:14.260 --> 00:06:16.930
It's simply impossible.

00:06:16.930 --> 00:06:21.720
Mr. Minister, I also want to ask you about
the threat of nuclear, because there's been

00:06:21.720 --> 00:06:28.170
a lot of concern over nuclear force or of
a potential nuclear accident occurring.

00:06:28.170 --> 00:06:32.770
In the past days, Ukrainian officials reported
a fire set off by a raging gun battle at Europe's

00:06:32.770 --> 00:06:35.740
largest nuclear power plant in southeastern
Ukraine.

00:06:35.740 --> 00:06:40.970
Putin, meantime, has put Russia's nuclear
arsenal as on alert as we know.

00:06:40.970 --> 00:06:48.100
Your country's foreign minister, amid all
of this, called it a bluff to try and influence

00:06:48.100 --> 00:06:51.150
both Ukraine and the West.

00:06:51.150 --> 00:06:56.470
How can you be sure of that, that Putin's
threat, that the use of nuclear weapons is

00:06:56.470 --> 00:06:57.970
just a bluff?

00:06:57.970 --> 00:07:06.690
Well, first of all, Russia — and Putin — is
using strategic communication very nicely.

00:07:06.690 --> 00:07:10.500
His major idea is to split us and to scare
us.

00:07:10.500 --> 00:07:15.630
And the fact by itself that we speak about
this threat simply means that he reached the

00:07:15.630 --> 00:07:16.630
ears.

00:07:16.630 --> 00:07:18.900
Yes, of course, he will try to threaten us.

00:07:18.900 --> 00:07:22.680
He will tell us that, ‘look, if you will
not give up this or if you will not give up

00:07:22.680 --> 00:07:26.250
that, we might use nuclear power because we
are a nuclear power.’

00:07:26.250 --> 00:07:30.750
But first of all, that would be disastrous
consequences for himself.

00:07:30.750 --> 00:07:36.150
And secondly, we are also, as far as intelligence,
observing what they are doing.

00:07:36.150 --> 00:07:37.840
We will know if he does something.

00:07:37.840 --> 00:07:41.070
At this moment, we don't have such type of
intelligence.

00:07:41.070 --> 00:07:47.130
But, but I'm asking you to just to just look
at the actions that he has taken now in the

00:07:47.130 --> 00:07:50.000
past weeks, and the words that are coming
out of his mouth.

00:07:50.000 --> 00:07:53.750
I mean, he has threatened, and I'm quoting
here "consequences you have never faced in

00:07:53.750 --> 00:07:58.850
your history" as he put Russia's nuclear weapons
on high alert.

00:07:58.850 --> 00:08:02.190
There's literally nobody between him and the
nuclear button.

00:08:02.190 --> 00:08:06.680
Do you really think he's behaving like a rational
actor right now?

00:08:06.680 --> 00:08:14.420
He's not behaving responsibly as a leader
or a president or whoever he is, of [how]

00:08:14.420 --> 00:08:16.160
a country with nuclear power should act.

00:08:16.160 --> 00:08:22.100
But, you know, still the situation even in
Russia is not that, for instance, Putin is

00:08:22.100 --> 00:08:27.030
waking up in the morning and he has a bad
mood, so he's just reaching the red button

00:08:27.030 --> 00:08:28.030
and pressing it.

00:08:28.030 --> 00:08:30.150
This doesn't happen even in Russia.

00:08:30.150 --> 00:08:37.790
So we very much believe that there is still
a chance to talk and let's say, to avoid such

00:08:37.790 --> 00:08:39.889
type of activities.

00:08:39.889 --> 00:08:46.730
And we don't have, in fact, other alternatives
because we cannot simply to give up to a bully

00:08:46.730 --> 00:08:50.959
who is telling "look, if you will not do this
or that, I will press the button, I will press

00:08:50.959 --> 00:08:51.959
the button."

00:08:51.959 --> 00:08:53.120
This is not how we can act.

00:08:53.120 --> 00:08:59.060
So as only chance is simply to keep cool heads,
to support Ukrainians in their freedom fight

00:08:59.060 --> 00:09:05.800
against invasion, and exile, exaggerate, with
sanctions, because these economic sanctions

00:09:05.800 --> 00:09:11.079
acts and will make Russia and the Russian
people reconsider.

00:09:11.079 --> 00:09:15.170
One of those initiatives that you have been
trying to pursue in order to support Ukraine,

00:09:15.170 --> 00:09:19.850
your president has called on the EU to stop
being "a political midget," that's the words

00:09:19.850 --> 00:09:24.830
that he used, and allow Ukraine candidate
status to join the bloc.

00:09:24.830 --> 00:09:28.870
Isn't it too little, too late for Ukraine
for that?

00:09:28.870 --> 00:09:33.380
You know, Ukraine — European Union, is large
but also a slow organization.

00:09:33.380 --> 00:09:42.259
But I would say that Ukrainians deserved and
paid by their blood already to get this accession

00:09:42.259 --> 00:09:45.170
country status.

00:09:45.170 --> 00:09:46.170
It will anyway take time.

00:09:46.170 --> 00:09:52.029
But I believe that one day, when this war
will be over, we will all be ready to support

00:09:52.029 --> 00:09:56.600
with something similar to Marshall Plan, to
recreate Ukraine.

00:09:56.600 --> 00:09:59.699
And I believe that they will be … members
of EU.

00:09:59.699 --> 00:10:03.860
Not today, not tomorrow, but let's say, some
three to five years.

00:10:03.860 --> 00:10:09.449
And that should be made possible because they
deserve this, they paid by blood for membership.

00:10:09.449 --> 00:10:12.220
So you don't think it will be just another
unfulfilled promise?

00:10:12.220 --> 00:10:16.029
Because I mean, they had the promise that
they would have NATO membership.

00:10:16.029 --> 00:10:19.079
They were promised that back in 2008, that
promise...

00:10:19.079 --> 00:10:20.910
No, no, no.

00:10:20.910 --> 00:10:27.220
There were no such promises and this was exaggeration
also from Russian side, because nobody seriously

00:10:27.220 --> 00:10:32.180
were thinking that Ukraine could become a
NATO member within the nearest ten years.

00:10:32.180 --> 00:10:36.170
So there was not even NATO plan for that,
because it was Putin's exaggeration.

00:10:36.170 --> 00:10:42.529
But about EU now, because of this war, I really
strongly believe there will be a lot of supporters.

00:10:42.529 --> 00:10:45.180
And Ukraine will be a member of the EU.

00:10:45.180 --> 00:10:49.410
Minister, just briefly before we go: Secretary
of State Antony Blinken said on Wednesday

00:10:49.410 --> 00:10:54.819
that the United States was keeping the door
open to diplomatic ways forward with Russia.

00:10:54.819 --> 00:11:00.540
Do you see any prospect for a face-saving
off-ramp for Putin right now?

00:11:00.540 --> 00:11:06.500
Well, not on the behalf of Ukrainians and
their sacrifices.

00:11:06.500 --> 00:11:10.220
If he wants a face-saving, he has to figure
out how to do this.

00:11:10.220 --> 00:11:14.839
If he withdraw his troops, if he stops the
war, yes, we might start to lift maybe some

00:11:14.839 --> 00:11:15.860
sanctions.

00:11:15.860 --> 00:11:20.389
But first of all, he has to do something,
because usually with Russians, it happens

00:11:20.389 --> 00:11:25.230
that they speak one [thing] and they do something
totally different.

00:11:25.230 --> 00:11:28.279
Such type of policies cannot succeed.

00:11:28.279 --> 00:11:30.749
Who could broker a deal with Russia?

00:11:30.749 --> 00:11:32.120
Excuse me?

00:11:32.120 --> 00:11:34.620
Who could broker a deal with Russia right
now?

00:11:34.620 --> 00:11:43.459
Well, I think we all, if we stand together,
Europeans and Americans, and actually I'm

00:11:43.459 --> 00:11:48.319
still looking forward what’s the big Chinese
response.

00:11:48.319 --> 00:11:52.640
Latvian Deputy Prime Minister and Defense
Minister Artis Pabriks, thank you so much

00:11:52.640 --> 00:11:55.889
for joining us on Conflict Zone.

00:11:55.889 --> 00:12:07.379
Thank you, madame, for inviting.

